+ * gather, read, compare) returns zero in every component and a zero
+ * sparse-residency byte, a size or count query returns zero, and a write is
+ * discarded. This is the behaviour the Metal Shading Language documents for a
+ * texture that was never set; it is stated here once so that one place says
+ * what null means. A level-of-detail query has no zero that is also a level,
+ * so it is refused rather than made up.
